  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>96</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi></math><br /><br />Frequency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>96</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> and that of <math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></math> function is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math><br /><br />In one-second cos function becomes zero at 96 times and second at 4 times. Hence net y will become zero 100 times in 1 second.",
